      "text": "The area of the parallelogram generated by two vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ is given by the magnitude of their cross product, $|\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{w}|$. First, we find the cross product of $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ using the determinant formula:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{w} &= \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\mathbf{i} \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix} - \\mathbf{j} \\begin{vmatrix} 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{vmatrix} + \\mathbf{k} \\begin{vmatrix} 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\mathbf{i} (1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)) - \\mathbf{j} (3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1) + \\mathbf{k} (3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1) \\\\\n&= -2 \\mathbf{i} - 14 \\mathbf{j} - 10 \\mathbf{k}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo, $\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Now, the magnitude of this vector (and therefore the area of the parallelogram) is $|\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{w}| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10 \\sqrt{3}.$\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram generated by $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ is $\\boxed{10 \\sqrt{3}}.$",
